<p style="text-align: start;">
  Hello,
</p>

<% if @first_year %>
  <% case @days_to_expire %>
  <% when 30 %>
    <p style="text-align: start;">
      We're reaching out because your <b>program expiration is coming up on <%= @expiration_date %>.</b>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      Want to continue on GitHub Enterprise? We're offering startups associated with an
      <%= link_to("approved GitHub for Startups partner", "#{GitHub.help_url}/enterprise/startups/partners") %>
      a 50% discount on GitHub Enterprise for their second year in the program.
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      GitHub for Startups Enterprise <%= link_to("features", "#{GitHub.help_url}/pricing/") %>:
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <span>&#8226; 50K Action mins per month</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; User Management (SSO)</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; Organizational Controls (SOC)</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; …and exclusive events, office hours, and webinars!</span><br>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <b>Interested in GitHub Advanced Security?</b> We're also inviting startups returning to the program and new to
      Advanced security a <b>50% discount</b> on GitHub Advanced Security!
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("Code Scanning", DocsUrlConfig.url_for("code-security/about-code-scanning")) %> - Search for potential security vulnerabilities and coding errors.</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("Secret Scanning", "https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/secret-scanning/about-secret-scanning") %> -  Detect secrets (keys, tokens, etc.) in private repos.</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("Dependency Review", "https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/supply-chain-security/understanding-your-software-supply-chain/about-dependency-review") %> - Show the full impact of changes to dependencies and vulnerable versions before you merge a pull request.</span><br>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
    To ensure your Enterprise plan is not interrupted, please <b>notify us with your intent to continue on GitHub Enterprise at
    least 5 business days before your program expiration.</b>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      Otherwise, your <b>organization will automatically be downgraded to a Free plan on your termination date</b>,
      and your Enterprise Account will be deleted. You will be notified once your organization has been removed from the Enterprise,
      at which time you may self-serve upgrade to a Team plan if you wish.
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      Thank you again for building with GitHub for Startups! Please let us know if you have any questions.
    </p>
  <% when 3 %>
    <p style="text-align: start;">
      We're following up as <u>your access to GitHub for Startups expires in 3 days</u>.
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      Would you like to take advantage of the <u>50% discount</u> for your second year in the program?
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      If so, we kindly ask that you <b><u>please confirm if you'd like to continue on GitHub Enterprise and the GitHub for Startups
      <%= link_to("partner", "#{GitHub.help_url}/enterprise/startups/partners") %> you're associated with so that we can send over a quote and next steps.</u></b>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      If not, no worries. <u>Once your termination is processed, you'll be notified when your organization(s) are removed from your Enterprise Account and downgraded to a Free plan</u>.
      Once that takes place, you'll have the ability to remain on the free tier or self-serve purchase the Team plan. If you receive an invoice for any consumptive add-ons, you will still be able to pay in the admin dashboard.
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      Thanks again for having been a part of GitHub for Startups!
    </p>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <% case @days_to_expire %>
  <% when 30 %>
    <p style="text-align: start;">
      Thank you for being a part of GitHub for Startups!
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      We're reaching out as your program expiration date is coming up on <%= @expiration_date %>.
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      At this time, we're offering you a <b>GitHub for Startups graduation discount</b> redeemable within 30 days of program graduation:
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <span>&#8226; Evaluation + GitHub Enterprise - <b>20% discount</b></span><br>
      <span>&#8226; Evaluation + GitHub Enterprise + Advanced Security -  <b>25% discount</b></span><br>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      GitHub Advanced Security:
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("Code Scanning", DocsUrlConfig.url_for("code-security/about-code-scanning")) %> - Search for potential security vulnerabilities and coding errors.</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("Secret Scanning", "https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/secret-scanning/about-secret-scanning") %> -  Detect secrets (keys, tokens, etc.) in private repos.</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("Dependency Review", "https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/supply-chain-security/understanding-your-software-supply-chain/about-dependency-review") %> - Show the full impact of changes to dependencies and vulnerable versions before you merge a pull request.</span><br>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <b>If you're interested in the above, please respond to this email at your earliest convenience.</b>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <b>If we don't hear from you, your organization will automatically be downgraded to a Free plan on your termination date</b>,
      and your Enterprise Account will be deleted. You will be notified once your organization has been removed from the Enterprise,
      at which time you may self-serve upgrade to the Team tier if you wish.
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      Thank you again for building with GitHub for Startups! Please let us know if you have any questions.
    </p>
  <% when 3 %>
    <p style="text-align: start;">
      We're following up as <u>your access to GitHub Enterprise expires in 3 days.</u>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      At this time, we're offering you a <b>GitHub for Startups graduation discount</b> redeemable within 30 days of program graduation:
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <span>&#8226; Evaluation + GitHub Enterprise - 20% discount</span><br>
      <span>&#8226; Evaluation + GitHub Enterprise + Advanced Security - 25% discount</span><br>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      <b>If you're interested in the above, please respond to this email ASAP.</b>
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      If not, no worries. Once your termination is processed, <b>you'll be notified when your organization(s) are removed
      from your Enterprise Account and downgraded to a Free plan</b>. Once that takes place, you'll have the ability to
      remain on the free tier or self-serve purchase the Team plan. If you receive an invoice for any consumptive add-ons,
      you will still be able to pay in the admin dashboard.
    </p>

    <p style="text-align: start;">
      Thanks again for having been a part of GitHub for Startups!
    </p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<p style="text-align: start;">
  The GitHub for Startup Team
</p>

<p style="text-align: start; font-size: small">
  <b>Resources</b>
</p>

<p style="text-align: start; font-size: small">
  <span>&#8226; Use our <%= link_to("Copilot-powered support", "https://support.github.com/success/copilot") %> and <%= link_to("GitHub Docs", "https://docs.github.com/en") %> if you need more help</span><br>
  <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("GitHub for Startups repository", "#{GitHub.help_url}/github/GitHub-for-Startups-HQ/tree/main") %>: information for templates and additional use cases</span><br>
  <span>&#8226; <%= link_to("GitHub Marketplace", "#{GitHub.help_url}/marketplace?type=") %>: shortcuts the open source community is adding</span><br>
</p>
